        "draft": true,
        "body": "Preserves the migration's accepted/pending frontier and recoverable work for a fresh session. Adds a continuation packet, progress checklist, updated accepted-unit ledger, and hash-bound data capsules carrying source history, actual control evidence, native/React preparation, and the separate advisory audits.\n\nThis is a documentation and preservation checkpoint. The retained control, native source, and future dependency/toolchain plans keep their unaccepted states; migration execution remains paused for the next authorized session. The maintainer explicitly approved publishing this source/evidence payload to KyleMit/Splotch.\n\nValidation: whole-checkout formatting, tracked documentation references and ADR integrity passed. An independent read-only Codex preservation review verified all six artifact identities, all 616 archive members, both Git-bundle heads/prerequisites, all 70 native intake rows, and unchanged migration worktrees. Historical application checks retain their original source/scope; no candidate execution is attributed to this checkpoint.\n\nDraft for review and integration into the long-lived migration branch. Refs #2690.",
